  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0158_781216d178ef.png\" style=\"width: 303px; height: 230px;\" /><br />First draw the given curves and represent the required area.<br /><br />Eliminate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">x</mo></math> to find point of intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">2</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">3</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">0</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>-</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Required area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>9</mn></munderover><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mn>9</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Hence, area is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>units</mi></math></p>"
